# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_render_interaction_honesty.py" "RENDER INTERACTION HONESTY GATE: PASS" "render interaction honesty (fork-clear copy + cluster.size crash)" "render interaction honesty (audit r4): two customer-surface render defects on the live render_pr_check. (1) HONESTY: the fork-redacted comment hardcoded 'This PR overlaps other in-flight work' for EVERY verdict, so a CLEAR fork PR that still posts a comment (a lane holder / shared-foundation / truncated) showed a 'Clear' header ABOVE an 'overlaps other in-flight work' body = a self-contradiction the external contributor reads -> _redacted_fork_comment now branches the coordinate line on verdict (clear gets a coordinate-neutral line that asserts no overlap; warn/serialize/unknown keep the overlap line); the redaction itself stays sound (no PR ref/login/path/symbol leaks). (2) NEVER-CRASH: a non-numeric cluster.size (a degraded/partial read handing back a STRING '3') raised TypeError on the \`>= 2\` comparison and took down the WHOLE render -> the App posted NO check and NO comment on that PR (a silent product failure). New _int() coerces the scalar field at both reads (the never-crash contract now holds field-deep, not just row-deep via _dicts). Proven on the real render_pr_check: a truncated/holder clear fork PR no longer contradicts itself, and a non-numeric cluster.size renders cleanly for clear/warn/serialize/unknown. content-free throughout" "render interaction honesty: a clear fork PR's redacted comment no longer contradicts its own 'Clear' header; a non-numeric cluster.size no longer crashes the render (the PR always gets its check+comment). content-free, never-crash field-deep" 24
